@page "/docs/api-reference/token"
@layout DocsLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Token — Vaultex API</PageTitle>

<div class="docs-eyebrow">API reference</div>
<h1>Token</h1>
<p class="docs-lead">
    Exchange an authorization code or refresh token for fresh access tokens.
</p>

<div class="docs-endpoint">
    <span class="docs-method docs-method--post">POST</span>
    <span>/connect/token</span>
</div>

<h2 id="content-type">Content type</h2>
<p><code>application/x-www-form-urlencoded</code>. JSON bodies are not accepted &mdash; this is per OAuth 2.0 spec.</p>

<h2 id="auth-code">Grant: authorization_code</h2>
<p>Exchange the code received from <code>/connect/authorize</code> for tokens.</p>

<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Required</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>grant_type</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Must be <code>authorization_code</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>code</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>The code from the authorize redirect.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>redirect_uri</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Same value used on /authorize.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>client_id</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Client identifier.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>client_secret</code></td><td>Confidential clients</td><td>Or use HTTP Basic auth.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>code_verifier</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>The original PKCE verifier.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Example</h3>
<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">HTTP</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>POST /connect/token HTTP/1.1
Host: auth.vaultex.io
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code
&amp;code=Abc123...
&amp;redirect_uri=https://yourapp.com/callback
&amp;client_id=your-client-id
&amp;client_secret=your-client-secret
&amp;code_verifier=ver_8a3f...</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="refresh">Grant: refresh_token</h2>
<p>Get a new access token without making the user sign in again.</p>

<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Required</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>grant_type</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Must be <code>refresh_token</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>refresh_token</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>The refresh token from a previous response.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>client_id</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Client identifier.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>client_secret</code></td><td>Confidential clients</td><td>Or HTTP Basic.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>scope</code></td><td>Optional</td><td>Narrow the requested scopes.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Example</h3>
<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">HTTP</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>POST /connect/token HTTP/1.1
Host: auth.vaultex.io
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token
&amp;refresh_token=RT_8a3f...
&amp;client_id=your-client-id
&amp;client_secret=your-client-secret</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="response">Response</h2>
<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">JSON</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>{
  "access_token":  "eyJhbGciOi...",
  "id_token":      "eyJhbGciOi...",
  "refresh_token": "RT_new_8a3f...",
  "token_type":    "Bearer",
  "expires_in":    3600,
  "scope":         "openid profile email offline_access"
}</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="docs-callout docs-callout--warn">
    <span class="docs-callout-icon">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M1 21h22L12 2 1 21z"/></svg>
    </span>
    <div class="docs-callout-body">
        <div class="docs-callout-title">Refresh tokens rotate</div>
        <p>The <code>refresh_token</code> in the response is a new one. The old refresh token is now invalid. Always store the latest one.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<h2 id="errors">Common errors</h2>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>invalid_grant</code></td><td>Code expired, code already used, or refresh token revoked.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>invalid_client</code></td><td>Client ID/secret mismatch.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>invalid_request</code></td><td>Missing or malformed parameter.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>unauthorized_client</code></td><td>Client isn't allowed to use this grant type.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

